{
  "$jdf": "1.0.0",
  "footer": {
    "content": "{{title}}  ·  page {{pageNumber}} of {{totalPages}}",
    "style": {
      "color": "#94a3b8",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 9
    }
  },
  "meta": {
    "author": "Ugur Kazdal",
    "pageSize": "A4",
    "title": "Why we built JDF",
    "unit": "mm"
  },
  "pages": [
    {
      "elements": [
        {
          "content": "OPINION  ·  2026",
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 4
          },
          "style": "byline",
          "type": "text",
          "width": 166
        },
        {
          "content": "Why we built JDF",
          "heading": 1,
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 12
          },
          "style": "h1",
          "tocEntry": "Why we built JDF",
          "type": "text",
          "width": 166
        },
        {
          "content": "PDF was designed in 1993 for laser printers. The web has since rewritten every other format on the planet — except documents.",
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 38
          },
          "style": "lead",
          "type": "text",
          "width": 166
        },
        {
          "fill": "#2563eb",
          "height": 0.5,
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 60
          },
          "shape": "rect",
          "type": "shape",
          "width": 16
        },
        {
          "content": "The problem",
          "heading": 2,
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 70
          },
          "style": "h2",
          "tocEntry": "The problem",
          "tocLevel": 2,
          "type": "text",
          "width": 166
        },
        {
          "content": "Every fix-a-typo task currently requires Adobe Acrobat ($240/year), a Word roundtrip, or some janky online converter. Every git diff on a PDF is meaningless. Every script that generates one needs a 200KB library to encode fonts as Type 1 dictionaries.",
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 86
          },
          "style": "body",
          "type": "text",
          "width": 166
        },
        {
          "content": "The premise",
          "heading": 2,
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 130
          },
          "style": "h2",
          "tocEntry": "The premise",
          "tocLevel": 2,
          "type": "text",
          "width": 166
        },
        {
          "content": "What if a document was just JSON? Open it in any text editor — clean source. Open it in a viewer — a rendered page. Edit either side, the other follows. cat, grep, jq, VS Code, every diff tool already understands JSON. There's nothing left to invent.",
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 146
          },
          "style": "body",
          "type": "text",
          "width": 166
        },
        {
          "content": "{\n  \"$jdf\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"meta\": { \"title\": \"Hello\" },\n  \"pages\": [{ \"elements\": [\n    { \"type\": \"text\", \"content\": \"Hi\", \"heading\": 1 }\n  ]}]\n}\n",
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 195
          },
          "style": "code",
          "type": "text",
          "width": 166
        }
      ],
      "id": "page-1"
    },
    {
      "elements": [
        {
          "content": "OPINION  ·  2026",
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 4
          },
          "style": "byline",
          "type": "text",
          "width": 166
        },
        {
          "content": "What you get",
          "heading": 2,
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 12
          },
          "style": "h2",
          "tocEntry": "What you get",
          "tocLevel": 2,
          "type": "text",
          "width": 166
        },
        {
          "items": [
            {
              "content": "A native macOS desktop reader (10 MB) that reads, renders, edits, and auto-saves."
            },
            {
              "content": "A 25 KB JavaScript library (jdfjs) that drops a viewer onto any web page with one tag."
            },
            {
              "content": "A CLI that validates against the JSON Schema and converts Markdown into JDF."
            },
            {
              "content": "A format that survives — JSON has no vendor, no proprietary parser."
            }
          ],
          "listType": "unordered",
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 28
          },
          "style": "body",
          "type": "list",
          "width": 166
        },
        {
          "content": "Embedding on the web",
          "heading": 2,
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 80
          },
          "style": "h2",
          "tocEntry": "Embedding",
          "tocLevel": 2,
          "type": "text",
          "width": 166
        },
        {
          "content": "Three lines and a tag — your document appears on the page, fully styled, scrollable, with a clickable TOC.",
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 96
          },
          "style": "body",
          "type": "text",
          "width": 166
        },
        {
          "content": "<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://unpkg.com/jdfjs/dist/jdfjs.css\">\n<script type=\"module\" src=\"https://unpkg.com/jdfjs\"></script>\n<jdf src=\"/whitepaper.jdf\"></jdf>",
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 116
          },
          "style": "code",
          "type": "text",
          "width": 166
        },
        {
          "content": "What's next",
          "heading": 2,
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 165
          },
          "style": "h2",
          "tocEntry": "What's next",
          "tocLevel": 2,
          "type": "text",
          "width": 166
        },
        {
          "content": "Editor plugins. Real-time collaboration over CRDTs. A rich-text inspector. A Figma-to-JDF converter. The format is small enough that the surface area of useful tooling is enormous — and JSON means the tooling already half-exists.",
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 181
          },
          "style": "body",
          "type": "text",
          "width": 166
        }
      ],
      "id": "page-2"
    }
  ],
